{%- comment -%}
  PG Cart Add-ons (2026-09-17): the cart upsells pg-cart-offer does not carry.

  pg-cart-offer paints ONE card for the newest product family in the cart and
  hides every other upsell row (the frame row included). Two gaps, by report:

  1. HOLO LEGENDS WALL ART. The Buy 2 Get 1 card shows and works, but the
     matching frame was never offered in the cart again, because its row is one
     of the rows pg-cart-offer hides. This file offers the frame in a smaller
     card while the cart holds more prints than frames (WHEN it gets the seat
     is in 5: the cart shows one upsell, never two). One tap adds a frame for
     every print that has none. Price and compare-at are read live from the
     frame product.

  2. R36 PRO 2 -- SWITCHED OFF 2026-09-18, by request: "hide the in cart
     upsells on the R36S Pro 2". PRO2_UPSELL below is false, so pro2Offer()
     answers null and none of the three cards in this note is painted. A cart
     holding only a Pro 2 shows no upsell (pg-cart-offer has no family for the
     Pro 2 and offers nothing when the cart names no family); a cart holding a
     Pro 2 and something else shows that other product's card, as before. The
     frame offer (1), the line pictures (3) and the one-seat rule (5) are
     unchanged. To bring the Pro 2 offers back, set PRO2_UPSELL to true; the
     code below is kept whole for that.

     What it did: the product has no family in pg-cart-offer, so a cart holding
     only a Pro 2 showed no upsell at all. Every Pro 2 offer is a VARIANT of
     the one product (Bundle x Color x Second Console Color), so an upsell
     here is a swap to a bigger variant and the till charges exactly what the
     card prints. No discount is promised that checkout does not apply.
       two Max Bundles in the cart .. Switch to the Duo Max Bundle (same two
                                      consoles, lower price)
       one Single Device ............. Upgrade to the Max Bundle (same color)
       two Single Devices ............ Upgrade to the Duo Max Bundle (the same
                                      two colors). 2026-09-17, by request: "if
                                      they add 1 console, upsell the max
                                      bundle, if they add 2 console upsell duo
                                      max bundle". It used to offer two Max
                                      Bundles, or upgrade only the first color
                                      of a two color Duo Pack.
       one Max Bundle ................ Add a 2nd console: the Duo Max Bundle,
                                      with a color picker for console 2
     One Pro 2 card at a time, in that order.
     THE CARDS NAME WHAT IS IN THE KIT (2026-09-17, by report: "what do you
     mean both cases in the upsell? Name them both"): soft rubber case,
     hardshell case, screen protector and joystick caps, the same four names
     the Max tile lists on the product page.

  3. THE LINE PICTURE FOLLOWS THE COLOR. /cart.js gives every line the image
     of the variant it holds. Each rendered line is checked against it and the
     picture is corrected when they differ, so changing a color or design with
     the in-cart picker always ends on the matching photo.

  4. THE UPSELL CARD HOLDS STILL WHEN THE LINE CHANGES COLOR (2026-09-17, by
     report: "when you change color on the cart it shouldn't change color in
     upsell"). Each Pro 2 card was keyed by the variant in the cart and drew
     that variant's photo, so picking Blue on the line threw the purple card
     away and built a blue one: the offer blinked and changed colour under a
     shopper who had only touched the line. Now:
       - a card's key names the OFFER (upgrade, second console, switch), not
         the colour, so a colour change re-uses the card that is on screen;
       - its picture is the first one shown for that offer on this page and
         stays that one, whatever the line does next;
       - the re-used card is handed the new offer (el.pgAddon), so the button
         still upgrades the colour the line holds NOW, and the words and price
         are refreshed only when they differ;
       - a colour picked for console 2 on the Duo card survives the change.

  5. ONE UPSELL IN THE CART, EVER (2026-09-17, by report: "there should only
     ever be 1 max upsell in cart, I have 2 right now"). This file used to put
     its card UNDER pg-cart-offer's, so a cart holding a Pro 2 and an orb, or
     any print at all (Buy 2 Get 1 plus the frame), showed two. The two files
     now share the one seat, by pg-cart-offer's own rule ("go off the product
     they added last"):
       - the Pro 2 was added last, or nothing else in the cart has a card:
         the Pro 2 card shows and pg-cart-offer's is hidden (its script keeps
         running, the card is display:none through a class on the slot);
       - a print was added last and the prints make whole sets of three, so
         Buy 2 Get 1 has nothing free to hand over right now: the frame takes
         the seat until every print has one, then Buy 2 Get 1 is back;
       - anything else: pg-cart-offer's card has the seat and nothing is
         painted here, unless after a grace period it turns out to have no
         card at all.
     A changed answer has to be read twice before it replaces a card that is
     on screen, so a read caught between two cart writes never flashes a wrong
     offer, and a stray second copy of a card is removed on every pass.

  6. THE UPGRADE BUTTON KNOWS ABOUT THE DUO PACK DISCOUNT (2026-09-17). The
     admin now takes $5.00 off each Single Device from two up ("R36 Pro 2 -
     Duo Pack Savings", the Duo Pack switch on the product page). The button
     on "Upgrade to the Max Bundle" printed the difference between list
     prices, which is wrong as soon as that discount is in the cart: the
     singles being upgraded stop earning it, and upgrading one of two leaves
     the other under the minimum, so it loses its $5.00 as well. Both sides
     are now priced as the till prices them. Nothing about the discount is
     hard-coded here: what it takes off is read from the lines' own
     line_level_discount_allocations in /cart.js, so a change in the admin is
     followed on the next read.

  HOW THE SWAP IS WRITTEN (the lessons are pg-cart-offer's): the new variant
  goes IN first and the old one comes OUT after, so the cart is never empty in
  between; and the old line is taken out by VARIANT ID through /cart/update.js,
  never by a remembered line key, because a line key on this store changes on
  every cart write.

  The cards use their own class (.pg-addon). pg-cart-offer removes any .pg-offer
  in the slot that it did not paint, and its heal() treats a surviving .pg-offer
  as its own card. They sit in #pg-unlock-slot so pg-cart-mobile lifts them
  above the pinned checkout pane with the rest. The button is a span with
  role=button: the base theme paints real buttons with a dark overlay.

  Registered in sections/header-group.json.
{%- endcomment -%}
<style>
